MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The smart plug feels like a useful next step because it would add lamp control to my connected home instead of duplicating something I already have.",
    "The Echo Show 8 interests me because its larger screen offers a possible way to view my security cameras, provided they are compatible. The Show 5 appeals for the same reason, but I would choose only the larger display."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The HD Fire TV sticks add little when I already have a 4K stick and a Fire TV television; a themed remote cover does not give me a practical reason to replace them.",
    "The Echo Dots fit the connected-home theme, but voice-only speakers do not meet my current interest in a display. Neither the tablet nor the SSD addresses a need I currently have."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My Fire TV purchases seem to have been taken as interest in almost any Amazon or Alexa device, although sharing that ecosystem is not enough to make me want something.",
    "Several recommendations repeat streaming or smart-speaker functions across different versions, while my interest depends on what useful capability a device would add."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My existing 4K streaming equipment matters: another streaming device needs a clear benefit beyond what I already use.",
    "My camera purchases make a compatible camera-viewing display more relevant than a voice-only speaker, and I would check compatibility before choosing it."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my connected-home interests but stretched them into broad interest in Amazon devices without enough attention to added usefulness and equipment I already have."
}
